{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Night at the Planetarium", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Getting Tickets", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future, in spoken interactions or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">May</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Can't</span> to Speculate about the Present", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the modal verbs <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">can't</span> to speculate or make guesses about something in the present. The modal you choose depends on the level of probability you want to express.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The grammar structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Level of Certainty\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"almost certain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it's possible\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"might<br>could<br>may\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it's very unlikely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">must</span></span> for logical conclusions. There is a strong degree of certainty about the present situation and it's almost like you're making the \u201cbest guess\u201d about something that's happening in the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">may, might</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">could</span></span> to speculate about things in the present when there are other possibilities. These modals all have the same meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">can't</span></span> when the situation is impossible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This movie <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be very popular.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I believe it <span class=\"strong\">might</span> even surpass Avatar as the highest grossing film of all time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">could</span> try using my credit card.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My credit card  <span class=\"strong\">may</span> be maxed out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> wait until next time. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> in the <span class=\"italic\">If</span>-clause to Express Polite Request or Refusal", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can ask someone to do something or refuse to do something politely by using <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">will</span></span> or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">won't</span></span> in the <span class=\"italic\">if-</span>clause. <br>Using <span class=\"italic\">will</span> in the <span class=\"italic\">if</span>-clause for these reasons is different from expressing future possibility. <br>Remember, an <span class=\"italic\">if</span>-clause is a dependent clause and cannot stand alone. <br>It must be added to a dependent clause to make a complete sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the following structures to make polite requests, and show insistence and refusal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">if + will</span></span>\u2192 polite request (this is similar to saying \u201cif you wouldn't mind\u201d)<br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If you'll just have a seat</span>, the doctor will see you shortly</span>. <br>(If you wouldn't mind having a seat, the doctor will see you shortly.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">if + will</span></span>\u2192 insisting that someone do something (this is similar to saying \u201cif you insist on\u201d)<br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If you will arrive at my house twenty minutes early</span>, you must expect to wait for me to finish getting dressed.</span><br> (If you insist on arriving at my house twenty minutes early, you must expect to wait for me to finish getting dressed.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">if + won't</span></span>\u2192 polite refusal (this is similar to saying \u201cif you refuse to\u201d)<br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> If you won't come to the party with me</span>, we can stay home and watch movies instead</span>. <br>(If you refuse to come to the party with me, we can stay home and watch movies instead.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Pronunciation Note</span>: When speaking and reading aloud, remember to stress the word <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">won't</span></span> a little more.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> you <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> do it, I<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> take it upon myself to do it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> you<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> do it, I<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> be forever grateful.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "proposition", "type": "name"}, {"content": "proposal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Listen, I've got a proposition for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about leisure.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to surpass", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go beyond", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I believe it might even surpass \u201c Avatar\u201d as the highest grossing film of all time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to flock", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to come in large numbers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:   People continue to flock to this movie even though it's two years old. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "maxed out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "at the limit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My credit card may be maxed out and I only have enough cash for my ticket and some popcorn. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hype", "type": "name"}, {"content": "discussion that makes something seem more exciting than it actually is", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I really hope this movie is worth all this hype!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to decline", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to refuse", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I tried to use my card before and it was declined.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le01ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or to your local library and look for information about the first movie you watched at a theater.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Find out as much as you can about it: date of release, premier week, how it did at the box office.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Reflect on when you watched it and how that experience was.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell your partner about the information you found and also describe the time you watched it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Express your opinion about your partner's movie.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I read information about a movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my experience of going to the theater.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about other's people preferences.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about science and leisure time.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  I can discuss going out and socializing.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain my opinion, and make and refuse polite requests using <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever wanted to go to movie premieres? Which movies?